          "section": "3.3",
          "title": "OAuth Token Management",
          "description": "- OAuth grants let third-party applications act on a user's behalf, and forgotten authorizations remain valid until explicitly revoked - Over-scoped grants give an integration far more access than it needs, so its compromise exposes data well beyond its function - Requiring admin approval for new apps and sensitive scopes stops users from authorizing risky integrations that bypass procurement and security review - Periodically reviewing and revoking connected apps removes dormant grants that attackers exploit through compromised third-party vendors",
