          "section": "1.2",
          "title": "Enable SAML Strict Mode",
          "description": "- Strict mode disables local password and social logins, forcing every login through your corporate IdP and its MFA and conditional-access policies - Leaving password or Google login enabled creates a parallel authentication path that bypasses SSO controls and is a prime target for credential stuffing and phishing - Centralized IdP authentication ensures departed employees lose Datadog access the moment they are deprovisioned, eliminating orphaned standing access - Datadog holds infrastructure telemetry, logs, and security signals that map your environment for anyone who gets in",
