          "vendorSlug": "gitlab",
          "section": "2.3",
          "title": "Harden .gitlab-ci.yml Configuration",
          "description": "- The .gitlab-ci.yml file is executable code that runs with pipeline privileges, making it a prime target for supply-chain injection - Pinning image and dependency versions, avoiding untrusted includes, and restricting privileged execution reduce the chance a build step is hijacked - A hardened pipeline definition limits what a compromised job can reach, containing damage to a single stage rather than the whole environment",
