          "description": "- Git lets anyone set an arbitrary author name and email, so unsigned commits provide no real proof of who wrote the code - Requiring cryptographically signed commits verifies that changes come from a known, key-holding identity rather than an impersonator - Rejecting unsigned commits and unverified users blocks an attacker from forging history or attributing malicious code to a trusted developer",
