          "vendorSlug": "mimecast",
          "section": "2.1",
          "title": "Configure URL Protection",
          "description": "- Malicious links are the most common phishing payload, and URLs that look clean at delivery are frequently weaponized after the email lands - Scan-on-click (time-of-click) rewriting re-checks every link at the moment a user clicks, catching delayed-activation and newly weaponized URLs - Newly observed domain detection adds scrutiny to throwaway domains attackers register hours before a campaign - Blocking malicious downloads and scanning internal URLs limits both initial compromise and lateral spread",
