          "section": "2.2",
          "title": "Configure Attachment Protection",
          "description": "- Email attachments remain a primary delivery vehicle for malware, ransomware, and macro-based loaders - Sandbox detonation of suspicious files catches zero-day and evasive malware that signature-only scanning misses - Blocking high-risk executable, script, and macro-enabled file types removes the most commonly weaponized formats by default - Converting attachments to safe formats before delivery neutralizes embedded active content while preserving usability",
