          "description": "- Enforcing SSO as the only login path closes the password-based side door that attackers use to skip the IdP entirely - Unrestricted exceptions let users authenticate with weak local passwords that lack MFA and conditional access - A tightly scoped, documented break-glass account preserves emergency access during an IdP outage without leaving a permanent bypass - Every uncontrolled exception is a standing weakness that can be discovered and abused long after it was created",
