          "description": "- Restricting account membership prevents unauthorized self-signup that would silently grant outsiders access to internal boards - Just-In-Time provisioning creates accounts automatically on first login, so an over-broad join policy can spawn unmanaged users - Explicit provisioning gives administrators a deliberate gate over who exists in the account and what they can see - Every uncontrolled member is an additional attack surface and a potential path to project and customer data",
