          "section": "2.2",
          "title": "Configure Session Security",
          "description": "- Bounded session timeouts limit how long an abandoned or unlocked session stays usable, shrinking the window for hijacking - Long-lived sessions on shared or unattended devices let anyone resume an authenticated session without re-authenticating - Forcing periodic re-authentication ensures revoked or deprovisioned access actually takes effect on active sessions - A stolen session token loses value quickly when sessions expire on a tight schedule",
