          "section": "2.2",
          "title": "Enable Multi-Factor Authentication for Atlas Console",
          "description": "- The Atlas console controls network access lists, database users, encryption keys, and cluster configuration — a single compromised admin login can expose or destroy all data - Passwords alone are vulnerable to phishing, credential stuffing, and reuse from prior breaches; MFA adds a second factor an attacker cannot obtain with the password alone - MongoDB's own December 2023 corporate breach began with a phishing attack, underscoring that console and identity compromise is a realistic threat - Authenticator apps (TOTP) resist the SIM-swap and interception attacks that undermine SMS-based codes",
