          "vendorSlug": "notion",
          "section": "3.1",
          "title": "Configure Sharing Controls",
          "description": "- Default \"Anyone with link\" and public-page settings can silently expose internal content to the open internet and search engines - Constraining guest permissions and link sharing ensures content is shared only with explicitly authorized people - Auditing and disabling unneeded public pages closes accidental data leaks that bypass authentication entirely - Notion pages frequently contain customer data, credentials, and strategy docs that must never be reachable by an anonymous link",
