          "title": "Implement API Key Best Practices",
          "description": "- API keys that send mail as your domain are high-value secrets, so storing them in a secret manager keeps them out of source code and config files - Keeping keys out of repositories closes the most common leak path, where committed secrets are harvested by automated scanners within minutes - Scheduled rotation limits how long a leaked or stolen key remains usable - Secret-scanning alerts catch accidental exposure before an attacker can abuse a key to send phishing or spam from your sending reputation",
